{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Shortest paths from one or more sources: for each reached vertex, its distance, its parent and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the edge from the parent (a forest when there are several sources).","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/sources"],"generated":true},{"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/distance(checkedTo:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/distance(to:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/distance(toIndex:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/hasPath(checkedTo:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/hasPath(to:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/parent(checked:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/parent(of:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/parent(ofIndex:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/parentEdge(checked:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/parentEdge(of:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/path(checkedTo:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/path(to:)"],"generated":true}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/shortestpathtree"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths"]]},"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree.swift#L29","fileName":"ShortestPathTree.swift"},"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ShortestPathTree","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ShortestPathTree","roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ShortestPathTree","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:13ShortestPaths0A8PathTreeV","modules":[{"name":"ShortestPaths"}]},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ShortestPathTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Distance"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","text":"DirectedGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Distance"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Comparable"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The first relaxation to a vertex’s final distance wins. So ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"parent(of: v)"},{"text":" is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shortest-path predecessor of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"text":" settled first. Vertices at equal distance settle in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unspecified order, so when several vertices at the same smallest distance lead to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"text":" along","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shortest paths, which one is the parent is unspecified. Among parallel edges from the parent,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the parent edge is the cheapest, and the first in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges(of:)"},{"text":" order among equals.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A tree holds a copy of the graph, so looking a vertex up never hashes on a representation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with cheap vertex indices. While the tree is alive, the next mutation of the original copies"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it; a tree of a graph about to change should be read and dropped first."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With several sources, each starts at distance zero ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".one"},{"type":"text","text":" over a semiring) with no parent."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Dijkstra’s algorithm and breadth-first search never improve on that, so a source keeps no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parent even when another source reaches it. Bellman–Ford treats the sources as one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"super-source: a negative path from one source to another improves the second, which then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has that distance, a parent and a path from the first."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Over a "},{"code":"SelectiveSemiring","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" a distance is the ⊗-product of a path’s weights, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"best by the natural order "},{"code":"<","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and a vertex is reached exactly when its distance is not "},{"code":".zero","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Not ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": two correct trees can choose different parents on ties.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://ShortestPaths/documentation/ShortestPaths/ShortestPathTree/parent(checked:)":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"parent(of: vertex)"},{"type":"text","text":", throwing instead of trapping when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" is not a vertex of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph: nil still means a source or a vertex not reached."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"parent"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"checked"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"G"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"VertexNotFound","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols14VertexNotFoundV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/parent(checked:)","type":"topic","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],